cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it and the accompanying paper."
title: "hornet-index: daily 1-km hornet activity index service for South Korea"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Min
    given-names: Sung-Hyun
    affiliation: "Apiculture Division, National Institute of Agricultural Sciences, Rural Development Administration, Republic of Korea"
repository-code: "https://github.com/Karl7208/hornet-index"
url: "https://karl7208.github.io/hornet-index/"
keywords:
  - Vespa velutina
  - hornet
  - honeybee
  - decision support system
  - Getis-Ord Gi*
  - GitHub Actions
abstract: >-
  Operational service that downloads daily station observations from the KMA API Hub,
  interpolates them to a 1-km grid of South Korea and computes species climate suitability
  (CSI) for five Vespa species, the Composite Wasp Risk Index (CWRI), the honeybee exit-activity
  index (BAI_E), degree-day activity windows and Getis-Ord Gi* hotspots, using the same index
  definitions as the paper code (verified by golden test vectors). Results are published daily
  as a static web map (national, staff) and district pages (citizens).
